# solid_sdd

This project uses solid_sdd for machine-checkable Spec-Driven Development.
Skills are installed via `gh skill` (typically under `.agents/skills/solidsdd-*`).

## Contract artifacts (defaults)

- ChangeBrief: `.solidsdd/change-brief.json` (scope premise / return point for the active change)
- Requirements (Gherkin): `requirements/**/*.feature` (property-level acceptance; not executable test SoT)
- OpenAPI: `openapi/openapi.yaml`
- GraphQL SDL (optional): `graphql/schema.graphql`
- OCL: `contracts/**/*.ocl`
- Derived contract tests: `tests/contracts/**/*.test.ts` or `spec/contracts/**/*_spec.rb` (dependents of OCL; not source of truth)
- Formal (optional): `formal/**/*.tla` (+ `.cfg`)

## Adapters

- API: OpenAPI 3.x (default) or GraphQL SDL — see `solidsdd-apply-api/references/`
- DbC: UML OCL → contract tests via `solidsdd-derive-tests` (Vitest or RSpec) — see `solidsdd-apply-dbc/references/`
- Formal specs (TLA+ / TLC): optional — `solidsdd-apply-formal` / `solidsdd-verify-formal`; early rollout **always** human-gated
- Language-native contract libraries: optional / deferred — never required

## Judgment defaults (tuned)

- Additive, non-breaking `api` / `dbc` with clear stack context → density `standard`, **no** human gate, confidence typically `medium` or `high`
- `breaking_change`, `money_boundary`, `low_confidence`, or `formal` `apply` → `human_gate.required: true`
- Shared mutable state / multi-client protocols → consider `formal` (`apply` only if TLC path exists; else `defer` with rationale)—never silent drop
- OCL `pre` failures must surface as a **named domain error** (e.g. `PreconditionError`), not only language builtins (`ZeroDivisionError`, etc.)

## Work decomposition

- Multi-criterion requirements → **`solidsdd-run`**: `solidsdd-brief` → ChangeBrief → `solidsdd-decompose` → WorkPlan (**one property-level Gherkin Scenario** per item) → **parallel** `solidsdd-loop` waves → integration `solidsdd-verify`
- ChangeBrief (`.solidsdd/change-brief.json`) is the scope return point (in/out of scope); when later phases are unsure, re-read or re-run `solidsdd-brief`
- Requirements use property-level Gherkin under `requirements/**/*.feature` (see skill `references/gherkin-requirements.md`); not free-form prose alone; not Cucumber SoT
- Single known slice → `solidsdd-loop` alone is enough (prefer passing a Scenario as the acceptance focus; pass Brief excerpt when available)
- Do not thin or rewrite `ChangeBrief` / `WorkPlan` in the parent; re-run `solidsdd-brief` / `solidsdd-decompose` if wrong
- Serialize loops in a wave only when items clearly contend on the same primary edit paths

## Adversarial critique

- After decompose / judge / apply-* / derive-tests / verify / apply-formal, run **`solidsdd-critique` as a Task subagent** (do not leave phase evaluation to the producer)
- Critique fails the loop only for **checkability holes** (unverifiable work slices, missing `pre` / error path, tests ignoring `pre`, density vs signals, soft verify)—polish is `minor` / pass
- On critique fail: feedback → re-run suggested skills as Task; shared **max_auto_retries = 3** with verify (per orchestrator); then human gate (no infinite loop)
- Details: `solidsdd-loop/references/adversarial-critique.md` or `solidsdd-run/references/adversarial-critique.md`

## Verification

- Do not treat work as done if API checks, OCL-derived tests, required formal checks, or required critiques fail
- API structural lint: `@redocly/cli lint <SoT> --extends=spec` when `redocly` is on PATH or `npx` works; if unavailable, skip that check (do not fail solely for missing Redocly)
- On failure: set `loop_action` and `failure_class` (verify) or findings (critique); follow suggested skills; **do not** weaken contracts to force a pass
- Default **max_auto_retries = 3** (verify + critique + isolation re-runs share the budget per orchestrator); same suggested skill twice with no progress → human gate
- After `solidsdd-run` finishes all items, run integration `solidsdd-verify` (do not skip)

## Human gates

- If `ApplicationPlan` or `WorkPlan` has `human_gate.required: true`, **stop** (before apply / before slice loops) until a person approves
- After approval, resume without thinning the plan (see loop/run `references/human-gates.md`)

## Execution (orchestrator / subagent)

- `solidsdd-run` and `solidsdd-loop` are parent-only
- From an orchestrator, run brief / decompose / judge / critique / apply-* / derive-tests / implement / verify / apply-formal / verify-formal as **explicit Task subagents** — never inline in the parent
- Do not thin or rewrite `ChangeBrief`, `WorkPlan`, `ApplicationPlan`, or `CritiqueReport` in the parent; re-run the owning skill as a subagent if needed
- Isolation violation → feedback and Task re-run (consumes retry budget)
- Details: `solidsdd-run/references/execution-model.md` or `solidsdd-loop/references/execution-model.md`

## Feedback

Rule thresholds evolve from project feedback. Tune judgment defaults and gate rules above; keep changes documented in the consuming project.
